WEBVTT

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.360
[music]

00:00:05.459 --> 00:00:09.442
Cool, so now when we
press play our spawn manager

00:00:09.454 --> 00:00:12.960
spawns one of our
obstacles, but we do need

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.799
to spawn more obstacles so
that way it's more like a game.

00:00:18.811 --> 00:00:21.600
So in our spawn manager script,

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.232
we're going to set it
so that we can actually

00:00:24.244 --> 00:00:26.960
create all of these
obstacles at intervals again.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:33.520
So first what we're going to do is we're
going to create another custom script

00:00:37.249 --> 00:00:43.600
so that we can spawn these obstacles.
So we'll call this void spawn obstacle.

00:00:45.589 --> 00:00:50.320
Make sure you put parentheses,
enter, create those curly brackets,

00:00:51.539 --> 00:00:54.916
and then we already
have a line of code to

00:00:54.928 --> 00:00:58.560
create a new obstacle.
So we're just going to

00:01:03.159 --> 00:01:10.560
take this entire line and we're going to
cut it and paste it into spawn obstacle.

00:01:11.519 --> 00:01:19.040
Now we're going to reuse that method that
we used before called invoke repeating.

00:01:23.309 --> 00:01:26.628
That's not in the
right place at all.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:30.960
That's better. So invoke
repeating, we'll use to

00:01:33.269 --> 00:01:37.465
constantly call our spawn
obstacle method over time.

00:01:37.477 --> 00:01:41.120
So we're going to use
the name of our method,

00:01:44.014 --> 00:01:47.870
which is spawn obstacle.
And we're going to

00:01:47.882 --> 00:01:51.840
give it a time to start
at. So in this case,

00:01:51.964 --> 00:01:55.760
we'll just call this start delay so that
we give our player a little bit of time.

00:01:57.299 --> 00:02:00.282
And then we're going
to give it a rate that it's

00:02:00.294 --> 00:02:03.040
going to constantly
repeat at. So we'll just

00:02:09.225 --> 00:02:11.136
call this repeat rate.
And then our computers

00:02:11.148 --> 00:02:13.200
matter to us because we
actually haven't created

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.543
those variables. So
we'll do a private float

00:02:17.555 --> 00:02:23.775
for the start delay since we know that
two is generally a good number to start at.

00:02:23.787 --> 00:02:26.640
So don't really need to
change that one around.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:31.117
And then for the repeat
rate, we'll just change

00:02:31.129 --> 00:02:34.720
this in code if we need
to. So private float,

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:41.956
repeat rate, and we'll
just have repeat every

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:45.200
two seconds as well.
Now if I go back into Unity,

00:02:47.955 --> 00:02:54.240
you can see that eventually we have these
obstacles that spawn and they fly very fast.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:57.696
Probably change that later.
And then there are player goes.

00:02:57.708 --> 00:02:59.680
Now one thing that
you might notice

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.867
aside from all the
obstacles that are just flying

00:03:02.879 --> 00:03:05.600
away in the distance
is that at some point,

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:08.537
our player starts to lean over
and that looks kind of weird.

00:03:08.549 --> 00:03:12.921
A really cool thing that you can do, especially
with rigid bodies is you can see under

00:03:12.933 --> 00:03:17.833
all of these different options for our
rigid body, there's actually constraints.

00:03:17.845 --> 00:03:22.240
So if I actually open up
constraints, we don't actually want

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:26.431
our player to be able to
turn or move in any other

00:03:26.443 --> 00:03:30.320
direction except the Y.
So we're actually going

00:03:30.321 --> 00:03:34.107
to just freeze the
position of the X and the Z,

00:03:34.119 --> 00:03:38.160
as well as freeze the
rotation of the X and the Z.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.685
And really we actually
didn't want the player

00:03:41.697 --> 00:03:44.196
to go up and down. So
that's just the Y position.

00:03:44.396 --> 00:03:46.867
So we'll just freeze
the rotation of the Y too.

00:03:46.879 --> 00:03:51.543
So now whenever the player gets hit by
an obstacle, they won't turn side to side.

00:03:51.555 --> 00:03:55.120
They'll just constantly only
be able to move up or down.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:04:00.253
So if we press play. And
then if I try and avoid these

00:04:00.328 --> 00:04:03.984
obstacles as best as I can,
and I just jumped over that one.

00:04:03.996 --> 00:04:06.560
And so then let's see what
happens if we run into one.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.709
Cool. And just get
hit by the obstacle.

00:04:08.721 --> 00:04:11.680
Nothing happens other than
that. I don't get these weird

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:13.386
tilts that happen
or anything like that.

00:04:13.398 --> 00:04:15.420
So perfect. That's exactly
what we're looking for.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.702
So now what you're going
to do is create your own

00:04:19.714 --> 00:04:22.800
variables inside spawn
manager for the start delay

00:04:22.801 --> 00:04:25.740
and the repeat rate.
You're going to take your

00:04:25.752 --> 00:04:28.960
instantiate method from
start. And you're going to

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:32.038
create a new custom
method called spawn obstacle.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:35.040
So then that way you can
just call spawn obstacle

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:37.517
whenever you need to
create a new obstacle.

00:04:37.529 --> 00:04:40.480
And then we're going to
reuse that invoke repeating

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:45.038
method that we had before
so that we can constantly

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:48.800
call spawn obstacle.
And it won't start until

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:51.588
two seconds and then
it will repeat every two

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.480
seconds afterwards.
And then last but not least,

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:57.852
you're going to use
rigid body constraints to

00:04:57.864 --> 00:05:01.440
actually freeze everything
except the Y position.

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:04.643
So that way the player
can only move up or

00:05:04.655 --> 00:05:07.920
down whenever they
jump. Now it's your turn.

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:13.240
(dramatic music)